!
! What was spent in a category this month, in Trebago (larder_rules.h
! LR1): closing - opening of the category's account, in integer minor
! units, one category per row, exact. Trebago does not hold the balances
! to a holder's range; spent.sutra does (0 to 18 digits), so a negative
! balance or one past 18 digits makes the two disagree and is held.
trebago spent
  in  opening(n), closing(n)
  out spent(n)
  spent(i) = closing(i) - opening(i)
end
